course: dictionary
lesson: 10545
title: The umpire in the game
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An umpire is the person who watches a game, makes sure the rules are followed and decides what happens. Umpires work in cricket, baseball, tennis, netball and Australian rules football. Umpire can also be a verb: to umpire a game means to be the umpire in it.
explain: «In netball a girl keeps pushing Maddie behind the umpire's back.» Behind someone's back means when they cannot see, so the umpire is not looking. «The one time Maddie shoves back, the umpire sees it and sends Maddie off.» The clues show that the umpire watches for rule-breaking and decides the punishment.
explain: In cricket the umpire's decision is final, even when players disagree. The umpire raises a finger to give a batter out. Players may appeal to the umpire, but fair play means respecting the decision.
fact: An umpire watches the game, makes sure the rules are followed and makes decisions.
fact: «Umpire» is a noun (an umpire, umpires) and also a verb (to umpire, umpired, umpiring).
fact: In football and rugby, the person in charge is called the referee, not the umpire.
fact: In baseball, the umpire calls «strike» or «ball» after each pitch.
fact: In cricket, «walking» means a batter who knows he is out leaves without waiting for the umpire, and not every player does it.
exercise: «In cricket the umpire raised a finger, and the batter had to leave.» What did the umpire do? | Bowled the ball to the batter | Ran between the wickets | *Decided the batter was out | Cheered for the other team
exercise: Which game uses the word referee rather than umpire? | Cricket | Tennis | Baseball | *Rugby
exercise: «Maddie wants to umpire the netball match.» What does umpire mean as a verb here? | To cheer loudly from the sidelines | *To be the umpire in the game | To play as a shooter for her team | To leave the court early
test: «In tennis the umpire sits on a high chair.» Where does the umpire sit in tennis? | On the bench with the players | *On a high chair | On the grass beside the net | In the car park
test: Why should players respect the umpire even when they disagree? | Because umpires always agree with the players | *Because the umpire's decision is final | Because the decision can be ignored | Because the umpire is their coach
exam: In baseball the umpire calls «strike» or «ball». What is the umpire doing? | *Making a decision about the pitch | Batting for the other side | Taking a walk around the field | Scoring a goal for a team
